# Build output. Note that Cargo.lock files ARE committed, including the one
# per excluded -capi package: pinning each shipped .so's dependency graph
# independently of the workspace is a deliberate release-engineering
# property of this architecture, not an accident (see "Workspace mechanics"
# in ARCHITECTURE.md).
/target/
crates/*/target/
crates/*/target-*/

# Generated language bindings (boltffi) — regenerate with `boltffi build`.
crates/*/dist/

# Built Python extension modules, produced by build-py.sh (v1 shared-liba,
# v2 capsule-vtable) and build-ft.sh (ft/ft2, the free-threaded pair). The
# .pyi stubs and test batteries beside them are sources. Globbed so a new
# variant directory is covered before someone commits one.
py/v[0-9]*/
py/ft*/

# Python virtualenvs, created on demand by build-py.sh / build-ft.sh. Globbed
# so a per-interpreter venv (venv-3.13t, say) is covered too.
/venv*/

# Generated ABI dumps. Deliberately NOT committed: libabigail's XML bakes in
# absolute build paths and per-codegen-unit hashes, so the file is
# machine-specific and churns by ~300 lines on changes that abidiff itself
# correctly reports as no ABI change. Stripping that metadata to stop the
# churn makes abidiff silently stop detecting real breaks -- see
# "Full ABI diff" in ARCHITECTURE.md. The hand-written *.abignore
# suppression files ARE sources and are committed.
*.abi

# .NET build output; the .csproj and Program.cs are sources.
cstest/bin/
cstest/obj/

# --- Local scratch -------------------------------------------------------
#
# A safety net, not a list of things this repo produces. Everything above is
# a known build output; everything here is the ad-hoc debris of working on a
# library like this one, which is what actually gets committed by accident.
#
# If you need somewhere to put a throwaway script, a captured artifact, or a
# previous release you are diffing against, use scratch/ — it is ignored
# wholesale and never checked.
/scratch/
/.scratch/

# Crash and profiling artifacts. This repository deliberately segfaults a
# harness (the DMA-BUF skip path) and runs it under valgrind and perf, so
# these appear in the working tree as a matter of course.
core
core.*
vgcore.*
*.core
perf.data
perf.data.old
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Patch and backup leftovers. check-abidiff.sh --self-test copies a tracked
# source file aside before patching it, and merges/rebases drop .orig/.rej.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*~

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.direnv/
.envrc
.DS_Store
